# The simulator makefile's output directory (makefile: BIN = BIN/, and every
# target invokes MKDIRBIN, so a clone without it builds fine). Five binaries
# were committed into it by accident; a build product in the tree is a second
# source of truth for something the makefile already produces, and it leaves
# the tree permanently dirty after any build, which is how a real uncommitted
# change went unnoticed through an end-of-session clean-tree check.
BIN/

# Precompiled headers. Upstream shipped sim_console.h.gch and it was removed
# in "Remove the checked-in precompiled header": on a fresh clone it is newer
# than its source, so gcc silently prefers it and a patched header has no
# effect at all.
*.gch
